      "title": "Finish with training, records and an honest process",
      "narration": "A new producer subject to Maryland's annuity training rule needs the approved one-time four-credit training and knowledge of the insurer's product before making the sale. This exam-preparation lesson is not that approved training. Required transaction records are maintained for seven years after the insurer completes the transaction. Each insurance company must supervise recommendations. A producer must not discourage truthful information, complaints or cooperation with an investigation. If a consumer independently chooses an unrecommended transaction, follow the specific acknowledgment and insurer review rules. The chapter has defined scope exceptions. On the exam, identify the client's need, relevant restrictions and the action the producer must take. Then check whether an exception changes the result.",
